1. Upstream Work and Derivative Attribution
========================================================================

PicNest is a derivative work of PicRand 2.77.0:
  Copyright (C) 2026 PicRand
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License, Version 3.

Major modifications introduced in PicNest:
  - Re-engineered the UI layer with Vue 3.5, Pinia, and Vite 6, adopting the
    warm-paper / golden aesthetic, floating island grid, and multi-theme palette.
  - Implemented an in-place direct linking architecture with virtualized 1024px
    display thumbnails, bounding memory usage under Chromium decoding budgets.
  - Introduced the two-tier duplicate detection engine: streaming MD5 exact match
    and visual AI verification with color block + pHash pre-filtering.
  - Built a zero-friction sandbox plugin architecture (Theme CSS and Renderer
    isolated HTML iframes with postMessage RPC).
  - Developed a standalone browser extension (MV3) for web image and screenshot
    collection via local service.
  - Added physical folder ordering with atomic two-phase renaming, hidden order
    prefixes, and `.picnest/meta.json` in-root metadata persistence.
  - Added an Eagle library migration wizard to reconstruct flat .library bundles
    back into hierarchical physical folders.
  - Completely severed and removed Steam status reporting, Steamworks runtime
    binaries, and proprietary telemetry to ensure 100% free software purity.

